<%# Sent by TwoFactorDisable after the user turned two-factor off with their password and a
    current code. Bare l(...) — EmailDateLocalization renders "Dec 08, 2026" in every locale. %>
<h3>Dear <%= @user.full_name %></h3>

<p>
  Two-factor authentication was turned off for your account on <%= l(Time.zone.today) %>.
  <% if @previous_mode_label %>
    Your method (<strong><%= @previous_mode_label %></strong>) is no longer asked for.
  <% end %>
  Signing in now needs only your password.
</p>

<p>
  This was confirmed with your password<%= " and a current code" if @previous_mode_label %>.
  Your firm's other company admins have been told.
  You can switch two-factor back on at any time from Edit profile.
</p>

<p>
  You are receiving this email because a sign-in setting on your own account changed — we always tell
  you when two-factor authentication is switched on or off.
  <strong>If you did not make this change</strong>, change your password, switch two-factor back on from
  Edit profile, and contact your administrator straight away.
</p>

<p>Please do NOT share this email with others.</p>
